# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Zydit TTS — environment schema
#
# HOW TO USE
#   • Local development : copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in values.
#                         (`cp .env.example .env.local`)
#   • Cloudflare Pages  : Dashboard → your project → Settings →
#                         Environment variables → add each variable for BOTH
#                         Production and Preview, then redeploy.
#
# SECURITY NOTES
#   • Never commit `.env.local` — it is gitignored.
#   • Everything prefixed VITE_ is embedded in the client bundle and is
#     readable by anyone who visits the site. Only put values there that
#     you are comfortable shipping to every visitor's browser.
#   • End-user API keys are NEVER set here — users paste their own key in
#     the in-app API Settings dialog (gear icon). It is stored only in
#     sessionStorage and wiped when the tab closes.
#
# MODEL ID: there is intentionally no env variable for it. The model is
# pinned in the frontend at `src/data/models.ts` (DEFAULT_MODEL).
#
# SIGN-IN GATING: controlled in the frontend at `src/config.ts`
# (REQUIRE_SIGN_IN). Set the VITE_FIREBASE_* variables below to make
# Google sign-in available; users cannot use the studio without it while
# REQUIRE_SIGN_IN is true.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── TTS engine ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Base URL of any OpenAI-compatible speech endpoint. "/v1/audio/speech" is
# appended automatically if missing, so any of these work:
#   https://your-gateway.example.com
#   https://your-gateway.example.com/v1
#   https://your-gateway.example.com/v1/audio/speech
# The endpoint must send CORS headers (api.elevenlabs.io itself does not).
# Users can override this at runtime in the in-app API Settings dialog.
VITE_TTS_API_BASE_URL=""

# ── Firebase Auth (Google sign-in) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy these from: Firebase console → Project settings → Your apps →
# Web app config. Full walkthrough: docs/FIREBASE_SETUP.md
#
# Auth is ENABLED only when API KEY, AUTH DOMAIN, PROJECT ID and APP ID are
# all present. When absent, the app builds fine but the sign-in page shows
# a "not configured" note.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=""
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN="your-project.firebaseapp.com"
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID="your-project"
# Optional — include if you want them baked in, but the four above are the
# ones that matter for Authentication:
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET="your-project.appspot.com"
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=""
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=""
